A1A","as_reported":"NM_001127221.2 c.2042_2043delAG, p.(Gln681ArgfsTer100)","cdna":"c.2042_2043delAG","protein":"p.(Gln681ArgfsTer100)","genomic":"","zygosity":"compound_heterozygous","origin":"inherited","consequence":"frameshift","key":"V4"},{"gene":"CACNA1A","as_reported":"NM_001127221.2 c.1693G>A, p.(Glu565Lys)","cdna":"c.1693G>A","protein":"p.(Glu565Lys)","genomic":"","zygosity":"compound_heterozygous","origin":"inherited","consequence":"missense","key":"V5"}],"variant_roles":["causal","causal"],"segregation":"Truncating variant maternally inherited (mother asymptomatic); missense variant paternally inherited (father with infrequent migraines, suspected mild learning difficulties); siblings not tested","inheritance":"AR","previously_reported":"","mixed_genotypes":false,"quotes":["Parental testing for these variants via fluorescent sequencing showed that NM_001127221.2 c.2042_2043delAG, p.(Gln681ArgfsTer100) was maternally inherited, and NM_001127221.2 c.1693G>A, p.(Glu565Lys) was paternally inherited.","MRI at 3 years (Figure 2b) showed cerebellar volume loss involving both hemispheres, vermis and middle cerebellar peduncles. Ventricles and extra‐axial CSF spaces were mildly prominent, reflecting mild cerebral volume loss.","Vineland Adaptive Scales, 3rd edition (Sparrow et al., 2016) composite score was 26, corresponding to severe ID."],"quote_grounding":[1.0,1.0,1.0],"followup_of":"","genotype_mode":"AR","genotype_reason":"biallelic variants"},{"id":"R:39416668:1","pmid":"39416668","label":"Child II-4 (index patient)","kind":"individual","family":"","n_affected":1,"n_families":1,"sex":"male","ancestry":"","consanguinity":"no","onset":"4 weeks","age_last":"died at 2.5 years","phenotypes":[{"text":"neonatal muscular hypotonia","hpo_label":"Neonatal hypotonia","hpo_id":"HP:0001319","present":true,"n_with":null,"n_assessed":null,"some_only":false,"other_cause":false},{"text":"severe muscular hypotonia","hpo_label":"Severe muscular hypotonia","hpo_id":"HP:0006829"